# WordPress PHP Conventions

See `launchdek-compliance.mdc` for the security gate.

## File Header

Every PHP file must start with:

```php
<?php
/**
 * Brief description.
 *
 * @package LaunchDek
 */

if ( ! defined( 'ABSPATH' ) ) {
	exit;
}
```

## Security

- Admin pages: `LAUNCHDEK_Capabilities::current_user_can( $cap )` — not raw `manage_options` except in capability class itself.
- REST routes: `permission_callback` on every route; delegate to `LAUNCHDEK_REST_API::can_*()` methods.
- Escape output: `esc_html()`, `esc_attr()`, `esc_url()`, `esc_html__()`, `esc_html_e()`.
- Sanitize settings via `LAUNCHDEK_Settings::sanitize()` as `sanitize_callback`.
- Settings API: `show_in_rest => false`.
- Never return decrypted app passwords in REST responses; mask or omit `app_password_enc`.
- SQL: `$wpdb->prepare()` only; all queries in `*_Repository` classes.

## WordPress APIs

- Register hooks in `LAUNCHDEK_Plugin::run()` or static `::register()` on service classes — not in bootstrap.
- REST namespace: `LAUNCHDEK_REST_NAMESPACE` (`launchdek/v1`).
- Enqueue assets with `filemtime()` fallback to `LAUNCHDEK_VERSION`. Plugin screens also enqueue `wp-components` (style + script) as a dependency for admin CSS/JS — powers `openConfirmModal()` via `wp.components.__experimentalConfirmDialog`.
- Localize `launchdekAdmin` with `rest_url()`, `admin_url( 'admin-ajax.php' )` as `ajaxUrl`, `wp_create_nonce( 'wp_rest' )`, and translatable strings. On the Checklists screen, also localize `customChecklists` (`preloaded` + `summary_list` items for non-template checklists) and `clientPreview` (`panelTitle`, `defaultPanelTitle`, `brandName`, preview UI strings). On the Sites screen, localize `sites` (`preloaded`, `list`, `groups` from `get_site_group_catalog()`). On the Activity Logs screen, localize `activityLogs` (`preloaded` + `sites` from `picker_list()`). On the Integrations screen, localize `integrations` (`preloaded` + `LAUNCHDEK_Integrations::get_page_bootstrap()` — `connectors`, `telemetry.rules`, `telemetry.fields`).
- Page slugs: use `LAUNCHDEK_Admin::PAGE_SLUG` + suffixes.

## Class Wiring

- Bootstrap requires all classes; instantiate only via `launchdek_run_plugin()`. `class-launchdek-admin-deep-links.php` loads before checklist/run repositories (used during step normalization). `class-launchdek-admin-ajax.php` loads with admin classes.
- `LAUNCHDEK_Plugin` constructor: `LAUNCHDEK_Admin` only. `LAUNCHDEK_Plugin::run()` also calls `LAUNCHDEK_Admin_Ajax::register()`.
- Data layer: `LAUNCHDEK_{Site,Checklist,Run}_Repository` — no direct `$wpdb` in REST handlers or admin.
- Remote: `LAUNCHDEK_Remote_Client::from_site( $id )` for authenticated requests (returns `null` if credentials missing). `request()` tries `/wp-json{route}` then `?rest_route=` when `is_rest_no_route_response()` (404 + `rest_no_route` code).
- Client panel: `LAUNCHDEK_Mu_Plugin_Installer::ensure_installed( $site_id )` on site create/update/test and when `push_run( $id, $prepare, $sync_bundle )` is called with `$sync_bundle = true` (defaults to `$prepare`; manual refresh uses `push_run( $id, false, true )`); `::sync_run()` → `push_run( $id, false, false )` (snapshot only, no bundle reinstall); token callbacks pass `$skip_client_sync = true` on `complete_client_step()` / `uncomplete_client_step()` / `add_client_step_note()` and return `snapshot` for client local apply; `LAUNCHDEK_Run_Repository::ensure_client_token()` backfills legacy runs; `::filter_step_notes()` / `::step_notes_match()` dedupe hub notes; `::archive()` / `::delete()` for run history (`is_archived` soft-hide); `::list_for_site_history()` for paginated lean site history with batched step progress; `LAUNCHDEK_Step_Executor::mark_manual_incomplete()` for hub-side manual uncomplete; `LAUNCHDEK_Auto_Capture::{get_status,start,stop,clear}()` proxies capture sessions to remote panel; `LAUNCHDEK_Settings::get_client_panel_layout()` / `::get_client_panel_layouts()` configure snapshot `panel_layout` (legacy `left_sidebar` / `split_panel` sanitize to `sidebar`); `::get_client_panel_title()` / `::sanitize_client_panel_title()` / `::save_client_panel_title()` configure snapshot `panel_title` (Settings form + builder `#launchdek-cl-panel-title` via `POST /settings/client-panel-title`); `LAUNCHDEK_Admin_Deep_Links::{resolve_path,normalize_stored_path,infer_path_from_text,path_from_api_step}()` resolve wp-admin paths for step deep links; snapshots include both `deep_link` (remote full URL) and `admin_path` (path only for client `admin_url()` rebuild). Client `LAUNCHDEK_Client_Run_Store::get_panel_title()` reads snapshot `panel_title`. Checklists screen enqueues `mu-plugin/launchdek-client/css/launchdek-client-admin.css` as `launchdek-client-admin-preview` for builder live preview only.
- Credentials: `LAUNCHDEK_Credential_Vault::encrypt()` / `::decrypt()` on save/read.
- Audit: `LAUNCHDEK_Audit_Log::log()` for privileged actions; `::query()` with optional `paginate`, `include_details`, `id` (site filter includes run-linked rows); `::find( $id )` for single entry; `LIST_DEFAULT_LIMIT` (50) / `LIST_MAX_LIMIT` (100); batch context maps in `build_query_context()` (users, sites, runs, step titles); `::format_row()` returns human-readable `message`, `action_label`, `details_summary`, `detail_lines`, `show_run_timeline`, `outcome_class`, `has_details`; `::format_details_summary()` / `::format_activity_detail_lines()` / `::get_run_steps_timeline()` / `::log_supports_run_timeline()` power Activity Logs copy; `::feed_entry_show_site_label()` / `::format_feed_message( $entry, $embed_site )` shape dashboard feed copy; `::log()` invalidates `LAUNCHDEK_Dashboard_Cache::invalidate_feed()`.
- Dashboard cache: `LAUNCHDEK_Dashboard_Cache::{get_stats,get_connection_counts,get_feed,get_quick_launch_picker}()` read from `launchdek_dashboard_cache`; `::refresh_quick_launch_picker()` delegates to `LAUNCHDEK_Site_Repository::picker_list()` and `LAUNCHDEK_Checklist_Repository::picker_list()`; repositories call `invalidate_stats()` / `invalidate_connections()` / `invalidate_quick_launch_picker()` on mutations. `::clear()` on uninstall.
- Integration sync: `LAUNCHDEK_Integration_Sync::{preview,sync}()` orchestrate connector site inventory import; when `summary.total === 0` and adapter implements `get_sync_diagnostics()` (MainWP), response includes `diagnostics.hint`; `LAUNCHDEK_Telemetry_Mapper::map( $integration_slug, $platform_row )` applies enabled telemetry rules; `LAUNCHDEK_Site_Repository::{find_by_external,upsert_from_integration,list_by_integration,count_by_integration_sources,ensure_integration_tag,normalize_url,has_credentials,get_distinct_group_types}()` persist synced sites and group catalogs; `LAUNCHDEK_Integrations::get_page_bootstrap()` preloads connector statuses + telemetry rules for Integrations screen; MainWP panel deploy without hub credentials uses `LAUNCHDEK_MainWP_Agent::install_panel( $mainwp_site_id )`. Site tag groups: `LAUNCHDEK_Settings::{get_builtin_site_groups,get_custom_site_groups,get_site_group_catalog,add_custom_site_group,get_site_group_label}()`; custom groups persist in `custom_site_groups` (Settings API sanitize on save).
- Notifications: `LAUNCHDEK_Webhook_Dispatcher::dispatch( $event, $data )` calls `LAUNCHDEK_Email_Notifier::dispatch()` first (wp_mail when event is in `email_notification_events`; recipients via `get_email_notification_addresses()`), then Slack/Discord/Teams webhooks when URLs are set and event passes `notification_events` filter. Email body enriches run context from `LAUNCHDEK_Run_Repository::find()` when `run_id` is present.
- Checklist summaries: `LAUNCHDEK_Checklist_Repository::summary_list( $args )` / `::format_summary()` return lightweight rows (`id`, `title`, `description`, `steps_count`, step id/title preview) for list/grid UIs; `GET /checklists?summary=1` (optional `is_template`, `is_vault`); `GET /templates/vault` uses `summary_list( [ 'is_vault' => true ] )`.
- Activation: `LAUNCHDEK_Activator` (sets redirect transient); `LAUNCHDEK_Admin::maybe_activation_redirect()` sends new installs to dashboard with `?onboarding=1`. Deactivation: `LAUNCHDEK_Deactivator` (clears drift cron).
- Legacy redirects (`LAUNCHDEK_Admin::maybe_redirect_legacy_templates_page()` on `admin_init`): `?page={slug}-templates` → Checklists (Templates default tab); `?page={slug}-sites&activity_logs` → Activity Logs page.

## Settings Option Shape

```php
array(
	'enabled'                    => true,
	'encrypt_credentials'        => true,
	'drift_verification_enabled'  => true,
	'onboarding_dismissed'       => false, // set via POST /onboarding/dismiss; cleared via POST /onboarding/reset
	'slack_webhook'              => '',
	'discord_webhook'            => '',
	'teams_webhook'              => '',
	'notification_events'          => array( 'run_started', 'run_completed', 'run_failed', 'step_failed' ), // also supports drift_detected, client_step_completed, client_note_added — see LAUNCHDEK_Settings::get_notification_events()
	'email_notification_events'    => array( 'run_completed' ), // independent toggle set — see LAUNCHDEK_Settings::get_email_notification_events()
	'email_notification_address'   => '', // comma-separated; empty falls back to site admin email via get_email_notification_addresses()
	'role_permissions'           => array(), // cap => array of role slugs
	'telemetry_sync_rules'       => array(), // array of { id, enabled } — see LAUNCHDEK_Integrations::get_default_telemetry_rules()
	'exclude_options'            => array( 'url', 'email', 'wp_environment_type' ), // REST field names; legacy option names normalized on save — see LAUNCHDEK_Settings::get_exclude_options()
	'client_panel_layout'        => 'sidebar', // panel display mode on remote wp-admin — see LAUNCHDEK_Settings::get_client_panel_layouts()
	'client_panel_title'         => 'Agency Checklist', // panel heading on remote wp-admin — see LAUNCHDEK_Settings::get_client_panel_title()
	'custom_site_groups'         => array(), // { slug, label }[] — Sites UI + GET|POST /sites/groups; built-in groups are code-defined
)
```

## Checklist Step Types

Steps live in `checklist.steps[]` (JSON in DB or template files).

**`manual`** — fields: `id`, `title`, `instructions`, `target_roles` (optional array of WP role slugs — UI metadata for agency assignment), `deep_link` (optional admin path — stored via `LAUNCHDEK_Admin_Deep_Links::normalize_stored_path()`; backfilled via `LAUNCHDEK_Admin_Deep_Links::resolve_path()` on save when empty), `show_note_field` (optional bool, default `true` — when `false`, client panel hides the per-step note textarea), `show_screenshot_field` (optional bool, default `true` when notes enabled — when `false`, client panel hides the screenshot attach button), `type: manual`. Executor sets status `awaiting_manual` and resolves admin path via `LAUNCHDEK_Admin_Deep_Links::resolve_path()` then `LAUNCHDEK_Remote_Client::admin_link()`. User completes via `/runs/{id}/steps/{step}/complete`; revert via `/runs/{id}/steps/{step}/uncomplete`.

**Step notes** (stored on run steps in hub `launchdek_run_steps.notes_json` + client snapshots) — array of `{ user, text, created_at, attachment_id?, attachment_url? }`. Notes require non-empty `text`. Hub persistence via `LAUNCHDEK_Run_Repository::add_step_note()` / `sanitize_step_note()`. Optional attachments reference existing remote media library IDs; hub stores sanitized `attachment_url` for display in Automation run tracker.

**`api`** — executed by `LAUNCHDEK_Payload_Mapper::execute()` using nested `api` object:

```php
array(
	'type'  => 'api',
	'title' => 'Step title',
	'api'   => array(
		'route'   => '/wp/v2/settings', // must start with /
		'method'  => 'GET',             // GET|POST|PUT|PATCH|DELETE
		'payload' => array(),           // request body for mutating methods
	),
)
```

Validate dry-runs with `LAUNCHDEK_Payload_Mapper::validate()` (used by `/checklists/{id}/validate-step`) — returns `{ valid, errors, warnings }`. `execute()` and `validate()` call `filter_excluded_payload()` for mutating `/wp/v2/settings` steps; stripped keys are omitted from the remote payload and surfaced as warnings (or `WP_Error` when all fields are excluded).

## Admin Deep Links (`LAUNCHDEK_Admin_Deep_Links`)

Resolves wp-admin paths for checklist step settings shortcuts (hub run tracker + client panel `.launchdek-client-step-settings-link`).

| Method | Role |
|--------|------|
| `resolve_path( $step )` | Full resolution: explicit `deep_link` → API inference → `infer_path_from_text()` |
| `normalize_stored_path( $path )` | Sanitize stored admin paths (not `esc_url_raw()` — preserves `options-general.php` style paths) |
| `infer_path_from_text( $title, $instructions )` | Keyword/regex rules for common screens (Permalinks, Plugins, Users, etc.) |
| `path_from_api_step( $api )` | Map `/wp/v2/settings` and other core REST routes to admin screens |

On checklist save, `LAUNCHDEK_Checklist_Repository` normalizes `deep_link` and backfills via `resolve_path()` when empty. Builder live inference uses `POST /checklists/infer-deep-link` (`LAUNCHDEK_REST_API::infer_deep_link()` → `resolve_path()`). `LAUNCHDEK_Client_Push::build_snapshot()` sets `deep_link` (remote full URL) and `admin_path` (path only). Client `LAUNCHDEK_Client_Run_Store::resolve_step_deep_link()` prefers the snapshot URL, then rebuilds from `admin_path`. `LAUNCHDEK_Templates::repair_builtin_deep_links()` runs once (`launchdek_deep_links_repaired`) to restore built-in template paths stripped by legacy sanitization.

## Built-in Template JSON

Files in `templates/{slug}.json`. Required fields:

```php
array(
	'title'       => 'Template title',
	'description' => 'Short summary',
	'category'    => 'security', // slug from LAUNCHDEK_Templates::get_categories()
	'version'     => '1.0.0',
	'is_template' => true,
	'steps'       => array( /* manual|api step objects */ ),
)
```

Unknown categories fall back to `maintenance`. New JSON files are picked up by `sync_builtin()` without re-seeding.

## DB Upgrades

`LAUNCHDEK_Installer::DB_VERSION` is `1.5.0`. `maybe_install()` calls `migrate_from_previous()` before `install()`. Do not reference `launchdek_workflows` or `workflow_id` in new code — use `launchdek_checklists` and `checklist_id`. Migration to 1.2.0 adds `launchdek_sites.client_agent` and `launchdek_runs.client_run_token`. Migration to 1.3.0 adds `launchdek_run_steps.notes_json` (JSON array of step notes). Migration to 1.4.0 adds `launchdek_runs.is_archived` (indexed tinyint; archive hides from default history). Migration to 1.5.0 adds `launchdek_sites.integration_source` and `launchdek_sites.external_id` (composite index `integration_source_external`). Hub notes persist via `LAUNCHDEK_Run_Repository::add_step_note()` / `update_step( …, [ 'notes' => … ] )`. `LAUNCHDEK_Run_Repository::all()` excludes archived runs unless `include_archived` is true. Audit log and webhooks accept legacy `workflow_*` action keys and `details.workflow` for pre-migration entries. Client panel audit actions: `client_run_pushed`, `client_step_completed`, `client_step_uncompleted`, `client_step_note_added`, `manual_step_uncompleted`, `run_archived`, `run_deleted`. Integration audit actions: `integration_sync`, `integration_push`, `telemetry_rules_updated`.

